model g9_reading_start
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "T, tally 2.1.2 (issue #46), G9: L §5.10 point 1, §5.19, E §4.2 steps 0 and 5: a reading's own place is tested at the points of the sign rule S builds (point 3, the close, is g9/reading_close). Point 1, a reading at a day's start, is in the day's first batch: ys (claims, min 0) stated at -5.00 PLN at 2026-01-15 start, padded from w_s, with nothing else that day, has its pad refused, <place> is <b> after the day's observations and plans of <d> (q_start); its twin zs, stated the same with top_s paying 10.00 PLN in that day, nets to 5.00 PLN and stands. Point 2, a reading after a decision, is not here: S builds no reading at an instant after a decision (M2, readings at instants). An opening always anchors: yo opening at -5.00 PLN is refused from the first batch's end, its opening instant reads as stated, and zo opening at 0 stands (q_open). tally 2.1.1 tested a pad's other place only: ys and yo stood at -5.00 PLN."

source fixture "T's fixture for S's kernel tests (invented values)"

source bank_feed "T's invented bank feed"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

place ys: claims PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place zs: claims PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place yo: claims PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place zo: claims PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place w_s: outside lives 2026-01-01..

place w_zs: outside lives 2026-01-01..

place world: outside lives 2026-01-01..

input amt: money PLN

input start_day: date

move top_s: transfers
  on start_day
  leg cash from world to zs amount amt

ask q_start: bal(ys, 2026-01-14), bal(ys, 2026-01-15), bal(zs, 2026-01-15)

ask q_open: bal(yo, 2026-01-01 start), bal(yo, 2026-01-01), bal(zo, 2026-01-01), bal(world, PLN, 2026-01-01)

version facts
  cite fixture
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 10.00 PLN
  start_day = 2026-01-15
  opening[ys] = 20.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[zs] = 20.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[yo] = -5.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[zo] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start

version statement_01
  cite bank_feed
  governs 2026-01
  known 2026-03-02
  pad ys from w_s
  pad zs from w_zs
  stated[ys] = -5.00 PLN at 2026-01-15 start
  stated[zs] = -5.00 PLN at 2026-01-15 start

ask zx1: explain bal(ys, 2026-01-01)

